c. Write a program to check if a given number is a magic number or not.
A number is said to be a Magic number if the sum of its digits is calculated till a single
digit is obtained by recursively adding the sum of its digits. If the single digit comes to
be 1, then the number is a magic number. Example: 199 is a magic number as 1 + 9
+ 9 = 19, but 19 is not a single-digit number, so 1 + 9 = 10 and then 1 + 0 = 1, which
is a single-digit number and also 1. Hence, it is a magic number. Print all the magic
numbers within a given range.
